WEBVTT

00:00:16.727 --> 00:00:20.772
<i>Like countless dreams being granted,</i>

00:00:20.856 --> 00:00:24.735
<i>words without any sense of realness</i>

00:00:24.818 --> 00:00:28.780
<i>A future form that resides in them</i>

00:00:28.864 --> 00:00:38.248
<i>can be seen in your faintly gleaming eyes</i>

00:00:40.459 --> 00:00:48.425
<i>When we passed by like
it was coincidence back then</i>

00:00:48.508 --> 00:00:58.101
<i>our encounter began,
serving as some sort of delusion</i>

00:00:58.185 --> 00:01:02.606
<i>ls fate laughing? I can hear it</i>

00:01:02.689 --> 00:01:06.151
<i>intersecting joy and pain</i>

00:01:06.234 --> 00:01:10.572
<i>Grazed by the voice I heard that day</i>

00:01:10.656 --> 00:01:14.201
<i>I held onto a two-faced strength</i>

00:01:14.284 --> 00:01:22.125
<i>Now I'll unravel that unsolvable reason</i>

00:01:22.209 --> 00:01:32.719
<i>and fly beyond the wish I arranged</i>

00:01:45.107 --> 00:01:46.608
"All cakes 50% off today"

00:02:39.161 --> 00:02:43.081
Say, Hamaguchi-kun and
I should come here sometime...

00:02:58.847 --> 00:03:00.432
Who are you?

00:03:00.515 --> 00:03:01.767
A Flame Haze.

00:03:01.850 --> 00:03:02.893
Fla...?

00:03:02.976 --> 00:03:06.646
I am the Flame Haze
with Nietono no Shana.

00:03:14.446 --> 00:03:19.576
What? Why is this little girl...?

00:03:20.202 --> 00:03:22.079
She's scaring me...

00:03:23.080 --> 00:03:25.957
N-No, stay away... Please...

00:03:26.041 --> 00:03:28.960
You no longer exist.

00:03:29.044 --> 00:03:31.171
A Crimson Denizen
has devoured your existence.

00:03:31.254 --> 00:03:32.631
You are long dead.

00:03:32.714 --> 00:03:33.423
Huh?

00:03:33.465 --> 00:03:38.345
You're a Torch. A replacement made
from the deceased's leftover scum.

00:03:38.428 --> 00:03:42.140
Deceased...? Me, dead?

00:03:42.224 --> 00:03:44.392
None of this makes sense!

00:03:49.189 --> 00:03:50.690
No...

00:03:50.774 --> 00:03:52.234
Stop...

00:03:52.317 --> 00:03:53.693
Someone...!

00:03:53.777 --> 00:03:55.153
Mom“!

00:04:22.681 --> 00:04:26.059
"Overture, Part 1 "

00:04:36.403 --> 00:04:37.654
"Ogami"

00:04:48.331 --> 00:04:49.708
Junko?

00:04:58.675 --> 00:05:01.178
I'm home.

00:05:01.261 --> 00:05:03.054
Welcome back...

00:05:10.479 --> 00:05:14.232
That human's reaction was a little odd.

00:05:14.316 --> 00:05:17.777
Mm. But she can't possibly doubt you.

00:05:17.861 --> 00:05:22.073
Humans can never
see through Torch disguises.

00:05:22.157 --> 00:05:26.036
Mm. I'm certain I inserted myself
into its existence properly.

00:05:26.119 --> 00:05:30.624
Plus, that Torch still had
a lot of power of existence left,

00:05:30.707 --> 00:05:34.503
so I was able to clearly determine
its connection to the world during life.

00:05:34.586 --> 00:05:38.632
The perfect disguise comes in using
that knowledge in speech and attitude.

00:05:38.715 --> 00:05:41.176
Without it, you will raise similar suspicions.

00:05:41.259 --> 00:05:44.095
You must gradually conquer your weak points.

00:05:44.179 --> 00:05:47.265
This isn't hard for me to
deal with. It's simply a bother.

00:05:47.349 --> 00:05:52.229
It doesn't matter, though.
It all boils down to slaying a Denizen.

00:05:52.312 --> 00:05:55.774
I'm here because it's convenient
for gathering information.

00:05:55.857 --> 00:05:57.442
That's all.

00:06:28.682 --> 00:06:30.767
The family lounge.

00:06:30.850 --> 00:06:33.186
I wonder if there's one here...

00:06:39.442 --> 00:06:41.236
Wednesday's newspaper.

00:06:43.863 --> 00:06:47.993
And, just to be sure,
I'll check the last two days' too...

00:06:48.076 --> 00:06:49.869
Huh? Where's today's?

00:06:49.953 --> 00:06:52.747
Junko. I'm about to start on dinner.

00:06:52.831 --> 00:06:54.040
Where's today's newspaper?

00:06:54.124 --> 00:06:55.000
"Huh?

00:06:55.000 --> 00:06:57.586
--Today's newspaper. Where is it?
--Huh?

00:06:57.669 --> 00:07:01.631
Oh, on the cabinet
in the Japanese-style room.

00:07:01.715 --> 00:07:04.092
Why do you want the newspaper?

00:07:04.175 --> 00:07:05.552
No reason.

00:07:09.347 --> 00:07:12.559
Oh, Junko. The cake...

00:07:12.642 --> 00:07:14.519
I don't want any.

00:07:32.996 --> 00:07:34.039
Here it is.

00:07:34.122 --> 00:07:35.540
Mm.

00:07:35.540 --> 00:07:36.916
"10 Years Since American's Disappearance- ♪

00:07:36.916 --> 00:07:40.086
"An American man who went
missing ten years ago in New York

00:07:40.170 --> 00:07:46.009
was found in Yosegi City's Joshi Park
early in the morning on the 15th."

00:07:46.092 --> 00:07:50.096
This definitely sounds
like the Torch we saw yesterday.

00:07:50.180 --> 00:07:51.097
Yes.

00:07:51.181 --> 00:07:58.313
To think a Torch on the brink of disappearing
would attract so much attention...

00:07:58.396 --> 00:08:03.109
The American man found in Yosegi's Joshi
Park after a decade-long disappearance

00:08:03.193 --> 00:08:05.820
has just arrived at Yosegi Police Station.

00:08:05.904 --> 00:08:10.367
This individual was a
famous model ten years ago

00:08:10.450 --> 00:08:14.954
and he was apparently found wearing
the same clothes as when he went missing.

00:08:15.038 --> 00:08:17.791
What's more, he has no
memory of the intervening time

00:08:17.874 --> 00:08:22.462
or any knowledge of why he is in Japan.

00:08:23.421 --> 00:08:26.383
We know that a Denizen is involved.

00:08:26.466 --> 00:08:28.718
But at what point did it devour him?

00:08:28.802 --> 00:08:29.844
Mm.

00:08:29.928 --> 00:08:36.309
He appears exactly as he did
ten years ago, and is now a Torch...

00:08:36.393 --> 00:08:41.398
The strangeness of this situation
has attracted a great deal of attention.

00:08:41.481 --> 00:08:44.818
You would expect the Denizen
to have gone elsewhere by now,

00:08:44.901 --> 00:08:47.529
fearing Flame Haze retaliation.

00:08:47.612 --> 00:08:52.492
Mm. That's why we came here--
to follow its trail.

00:08:52.575 --> 00:08:54.160
But, this is a shock.

00:08:56.538 --> 00:08:59.499
I can't believe it's still in this city...

00:09:06.548 --> 00:09:08.425
Welcome home.

00:09:08.508 --> 00:09:11.970
You look glum.
ls Junko still miffed at you?

00:09:12.053 --> 00:09:13.888
Very much so.

00:09:13.972 --> 00:09:18.852
But it's okay. I know she'll
understand once I can explain to her.

00:09:18.935 --> 00:09:20.103
Yeah.

00:09:21.688 --> 00:09:25.650
The energy indicating the
Denizen's strength is miniscule.

00:09:25.733 --> 00:09:28.945
It's difficult to believe one
this weak would remain here,

00:09:29.028 --> 00:09:32.157
unafraid of Flame Hazes.

00:09:32.240 --> 00:09:33.825
It's definitely here.

00:09:33.908 --> 00:09:37.662
In spite of that, there are too few Torches.

00:09:37.746 --> 00:09:38.621
Yes.

00:09:38.705 --> 00:09:42.959
We spent half a day searching
and only found a single Torch.

00:09:57.390 --> 00:10:00.185
Junko Ogami is our only lead.

00:10:00.268 --> 00:10:04.439
But it's anyone's guess when
or where she ran into the Denizen.

00:10:04.522 --> 00:10:06.733
Junko. Dinner.

00:10:06.816 --> 00:10:12.030
Junko Ogami's family might
know if she changed at all recently.

00:10:12.113 --> 00:10:14.199
Junko? Did you hear me?

00:10:14.282 --> 00:10:18.036
Do not waste this advantage
of being in the Torch's existence.

00:10:18.119 --> 00:10:22.624
By adopting the proper attitude,
you can investigate in peace.

00:10:22.707 --> 00:10:24.083
Understood.

00:10:38.932 --> 00:10:41.434
Junko Ogami's father.

00:10:41.518 --> 00:10:43.102
I'm home.

00:10:46.189 --> 00:10:48.566
That's your mother's seat.

00:10:48.650 --> 00:10:51.945
You don't care that you can't see the TV?

00:10:52.028 --> 00:10:53.029
No.

00:10:53.112 --> 00:10:54.656
Is something the matter?

00:10:54.739 --> 00:10:56.115
Not really.

00:10:56.199 --> 00:10:57.575
I see.

00:10:59.661 --> 00:11:04.082
Interacting with humans is such a pain.

00:11:04.165 --> 00:11:07.418
Has anything been different about me lately?

00:11:10.964 --> 00:11:12.882
Err...

00:11:12.966 --> 00:11:15.093
The stew will be ready in a minute!

00:11:15.176 --> 00:11:17.428
Oh, that's great.

00:11:17.512 --> 00:11:20.223
Today was a little chilly and all.

00:11:23.977 --> 00:11:25.562
Junko.

00:11:25.645 --> 00:11:27.021
Listen...

00:11:27.105 --> 00:11:29.232
Your mother didn't mean any offense.

00:11:29.315 --> 00:11:31.109
Forgive her, okay?

00:11:35.697 --> 00:11:39.784
It's just, umm...

00:11:39.867 --> 00:11:44.873
Seeing her daughter doing that sort
of thing in public threw her off guard.

00:11:44.956 --> 00:11:47.959
So, this Hama-- What was it again?

00:11:48.042 --> 00:11:49.836
Hamaguchi-kun?

00:11:50.670 --> 00:11:53.006
Your mother's really down in the dumps.

00:11:53.089 --> 00:11:56.676
Don't be so cross with her, okay?

00:11:56.759 --> 00:11:59.345
Junko. Are you listening?

00:11:59.429 --> 00:12:01.306
Is that what's been different lately?

00:12:01.389 --> 00:12:02.307
Huh?

00:12:02.390 --> 00:12:04.434
Here we are!

00:12:04.517 --> 00:12:07.145
Oh? Huh? The newspaper...

00:12:07.228 --> 00:12:09.564
Oh, right. For a pot stand.

00:12:34.130 --> 00:12:36.090
Thank you, Junko!

00:12:38.509 --> 00:12:42.805
So, to ask again,
has anything else been different?

00:12:42.889 --> 00:12:45.141
Have I stood around with
a spaced-out look,

00:12:45.224 --> 00:12:49.437
or have you forgotten that
I'm here or anything like that?

00:12:49.520 --> 00:12:50.897
Huh?

00:12:56.611 --> 00:13:00.698
That certainly wasn't a
completely peaceful questioning.

00:13:00.782 --> 00:13:04.911
Given the amount of power of
existence Junko Ogami had as a Torch,

00:13:04.994 --> 00:13:10.291
you should have a grasp of her proper
behavior too, not just her close ties.

00:13:10.375 --> 00:13:12.168
I hate beating around the bush.

00:13:12.251 --> 00:13:14.837
The scarcity of information
is the real issue here.

00:13:14.921 --> 00:13:19.884
Mm. The parents provided
almost no helpful information.

00:13:19.968 --> 00:13:24.180
No excursions, and no unusual behavior.

00:13:24.263 --> 00:13:26.349
All we have to go on is that she and her mother

00:13:26.432 --> 00:13:28.851
had an argument three days ago, on Tuesday.

00:13:28.935 --> 00:13:30.728
Yukio Hamaguchi...

00:13:30.812 --> 00:13:33.982
Junko Ogami's high school classmate.

00:13:36.067 --> 00:13:38.152
I wonder if he's connected to the Denizen...

00:13:38.236 --> 00:13:41.781
Your only choice is to
find out at school tomorrow.

00:13:41.864 --> 00:13:43.241
Mm.

00:14:03.177 --> 00:14:04.345
What's the matter with her?

00:14:04.429 --> 00:14:08.391
She's likely upset about
her argument with Junko Ogami.

00:14:09.684 --> 00:14:12.353
She'll forget soon enough.

00:14:12.437 --> 00:14:17.900
Once I leave this city, Junko Ogami's
existence will completely vanish,

00:14:17.984 --> 00:14:20.319
meaning she'll never have existed.

00:14:22.447 --> 00:14:25.408
She'll forget she even had a daughter.

00:14:25.491 --> 00:14:28.411
There's nothing to worry about.

00:15:29.388 --> 00:15:34.060
Junko Ogami, Class 2-3, Student #2.

00:15:47.198 --> 00:15:48.491
--Good morning, Junko!

00:15:48.491 --> 00:15:49.158
--You came!
--Good morning, Junko!

00:15:49.200 --> 00:15:51.202
It's the lovey-dovey girl!

00:15:51.285 --> 00:15:52.495
Annoying-

00:15:52.578 --> 00:15:56.165
You managed to get away yesterday,
but today you're going to talk!

00:15:56.249 --> 00:15:58.084
So, how did it go?

00:15:58.167 --> 00:16:00.336
You can't keep us in the dark!

00:16:00.419 --> 00:16:01.712
Huh? What?

00:16:01.796 --> 00:16:03.673
Oh, you! You're playing dumb!

00:16:03.756 --> 00:16:05.716
We're talking about you
and Hamaguchi, obviously!

00:16:05.800 --> 00:16:07.343
It's not nice to keep secrets!

00:16:07.426 --> 00:16:08.261
--Hamaguchi...

00:16:08.261 --> 00:16:08.886
--Out with it!
--Hamaguchi...

00:16:08.928 --> 00:16:11.264
--Tell us!
--Do they mean Yukio Hamaguchi?

00:16:11.347 --> 00:16:13.474
I'm the one who wanted to ask that...

00:16:13.558 --> 00:16:17.603
What did Junko Ogami and
Yukio Hamaguchi do together?

00:16:17.687 --> 00:16:26.779
Seeing her daughter doing that
sort of thing in public threw her off guard.

00:16:26.863 --> 00:16:29.157
What could "that sort of thing" be?

00:16:29.240 --> 00:16:32.535
At any rate, there's definitely
some sort of secret involved in this.

00:16:33.953 --> 00:16:35.162
Where's Yukio Hamaguchi?

00:16:35.246 --> 00:16:37.582
Oh? Crying out for help already?

00:16:37.665 --> 00:16:39.876
Man! You really know how to show off!

00:16:39.959 --> 00:16:41.460
I wish I was so lucky!

00:16:41.544 --> 00:16:42.795
What's with these girls?

00:16:42.879 --> 00:16:43.838
--They're exhausting...
--Morning!

00:16:43.921 --> 00:16:46.173
Oh, speak of the devil!

00:16:52.889 --> 00:16:54.682
What is this?

00:16:59.937 --> 00:17:00.855
--Good morning!

00:17:00.855 --> 00:17:02.607
--Morning!
--Good morning!

00:17:02.690 --> 00:17:06.277
Yukio Hamaguchi...

00:17:06.360 --> 00:17:07.737
Morning!

00:17:08.905 --> 00:17:09.822
Something wrong?

00:17:09.906 --> 00:17:12.408
Wow! A passionate gaze first
thing in the morning!

00:17:12.491 --> 00:17:14.702
Hamaguchi's totally love-drunk too!

00:17:14.785 --> 00:17:16.120
I'm so jealous!

00:17:16.203 --> 00:17:18.581
Tell this facility's instructor-the teacher--

00:17:18.664 --> 00:17:22.335
that I'm leaving early
today due to a sudden illness.

00:17:22.418 --> 00:17:23.586
Huh?

00:17:23.669 --> 00:17:27.214
You're the most acquainted
with Ogami Junko's activities, yes?

00:17:27.298 --> 00:17:27.965
Huh?

00:17:28.007 --> 00:17:30.676
I have questions for you.
Let's go where we won't be disturbed.

00:17:30.760 --> 00:17:32.011
Huh? Whoa! Hey!

00:17:32.094 --> 00:17:33.429
Hey! Wait, Junko!

00:17:33.512 --> 00:17:34.805
Hey class is about to start!

00:17:34.889 --> 00:17:36.557
Wow! They're eloping!

00:17:36.641 --> 00:17:40.311
Come on, Junko!

00:17:40.394 --> 00:17:41.979
H-Hey!

00:17:49.028 --> 00:17:51.447
Geez... What's up with you?

00:17:51.530 --> 00:17:54.742
I told you already.
I have questions for you.

00:17:54.825 --> 00:17:57.620
Huh? Again, what's up with you?

00:18:05.044 --> 00:18:09.840
Ridiculous. This is the one
human I don't need to hesitate with.

00:18:09.924 --> 00:18:13.219
Tell me everything I've
done over the past several days.

00:18:13.302 --> 00:18:14.220
Huh?

00:18:14.303 --> 00:18:16.555
So you did get chewed out?

00:18:16.639 --> 00:18:17.723
Huh?

00:18:17.807 --> 00:18:20.476
Did you get into another argument?

00:18:20.559 --> 00:18:23.229
Umm...

00:18:23.312 --> 00:18:26.065
How can I answer to make him talk?

00:18:26.148 --> 00:18:29.902
They asked you all about us, didn't they?

00:18:29.986 --> 00:18:33.197
But, it's like, what else
is there to say, you know?

00:18:33.280 --> 00:18:36.659
It's not like we're gallivanting
all over the place or anything.

00:18:36.742 --> 00:18:38.869
Besides, that time at Joshi Park...

00:18:39.829 --> 00:18:43.040
That was the first time.

00:18:43.124 --> 00:18:47.003
Her father said they did something,

00:18:47.086 --> 00:18:50.965
but judging by things here,
it couldn't have been that bad.

00:18:51.048 --> 00:18:53.676
What did they do, then?

00:18:53.759 --> 00:18:57.763
I'm really sorry. It's my fault
your parents got on your case.

00:18:57.847 --> 00:19:02.018
Is there a connection
with what she and Yukio did

00:19:02.101 --> 00:19:05.479
three days ago at Joshi Park?

00:19:05.563 --> 00:19:06.981
--Joshi Park...

00:19:06.981 --> 00:19:07.273
--Huh?
--Joshi Park...

00:19:07.273 --> 00:19:08.607
--Huh?
Joshi Park!

00:19:08.691 --> 00:19:14.530
The American man found in Yosegi's Joshi
Park after a decade-long disappearance--

00:19:14.613 --> 00:19:15.906
--What about Joshi Park?

00:19:15.906 --> 00:19:17.366
--The same place...
--What about Joshi Park?

00:19:17.450 --> 00:19:19.160
It's not much, but it's a connection.

00:19:19.243 --> 00:19:20.911
Hey! Earth to Junko!

00:19:20.995 --> 00:19:23.122
Huh? Oh.

00:19:23.205 --> 00:19:25.833
What's wrong? You're spacing out again.

00:19:25.916 --> 00:19:28.252
Again? What do you mean by that?!

00:19:28.335 --> 00:19:29.420
Oh, sorry.

00:19:29.503 --> 00:19:32.006
I'm not angry. I want to know.

00:19:32.089 --> 00:19:34.216
When was I like that before?

00:19:34.300 --> 00:19:37.636
Don't you remember?

00:19:37.720 --> 00:19:42.099
You went to the restroom at
Joshi Park but never came back.

00:19:42.183 --> 00:19:44.935
I thought you had gotten lost,
so I went to look for you.

00:19:45.019 --> 00:19:47.605
You were standing by the pond,
completely spacing out,

00:19:47.688 --> 00:19:51.942
and I actually passed right by
you without noticing you right away...

00:19:53.360 --> 00:19:56.739
He didn't notice her despite being nearby?

00:19:56.822 --> 00:20:00.743
I've found it. The moment
she became a Torch.

00:20:00.826 --> 00:20:03.454
Three days ago, in Joshi Park,

00:20:03.537 --> 00:20:08.334
Junko Ogami was devoured
by a Denizen and became a Torch.

00:20:14.256 --> 00:20:16.592
Junko? Are you sure you're okay?

00:20:16.675 --> 00:20:19.720
Tell me more about
what happened in Joshi Park.

00:20:19.804 --> 00:20:23.766
What happened there,
what we did there... Everything!

00:21:03.931 --> 00:21:07.435
It's very likely that
Yukio Hamaguchi and Junko Ogami

00:21:07.518 --> 00:21:10.187
encountered a Denizen in Joshi Park.

00:21:10.271 --> 00:21:11.230
Mm.

00:21:11.313 --> 00:21:14.483
But only Junko Ogami was devoured.

00:21:14.567 --> 00:21:19.029
There's too much out of
the ordinary about this Denizen...

00:21:19.113 --> 00:21:22.908
Perhaps visiting Joshi Park
with Yukio Hamaguchi tomorrow

00:21:22.992 --> 00:21:25.661
will shed some light on things.

00:21:31.709 --> 00:21:33.294
Welcome home.

00:21:33.711 --> 00:21:35.087
There's cake.

00:21:35.171 --> 00:21:36.338
Cake?

00:21:36.422 --> 00:21:39.383
Well, yesterday's cake was squished, so...

00:21:56.942 --> 00:22:01.197
You're all grown up now,
but you're still a little girl deep down.

00:22:07.870 --> 00:22:13.792
You still get your food everywhere when
you eat. You haven't changed at all.

00:22:13.876 --> 00:22:16.086
Really?

00:22:16.170 --> 00:22:17.588
Yes.

00:22:17.671 --> 00:22:24.094
You'd dive under my blanket whenever
you got scared at night, remember?

00:22:24.178 --> 00:22:26.096
You're still like that.

00:22:26.180 --> 00:22:28.098
You were a real scaredy-cat.

00:22:28.182 --> 00:22:32.144
Whenever there was lightning
or a big storm or a scary TV show,

00:22:32.228 --> 00:22:38.150
you'd already be in bed with me by
the time I noticed my door was open.

00:22:38.234 --> 00:22:43.447
The Junko Ogami this mother
is speaking of is dead now.

00:22:43.530 --> 00:22:47.826
She doesn't know that.

00:22:47.910 --> 00:22:52.331
You did that to ease your loneliness
when your brother moved out, too.

00:22:53.749 --> 00:22:55.334
Loneliness...

00:22:55.417 --> 00:22:59.505
I run when I'm lonely too?
Just like when I'm scared?

00:22:59.588 --> 00:23:05.511
Hmm, it's not so much "running"
as it is trying to be with me, I'd say.

00:23:05.594 --> 00:23:06.971
With you...

00:23:08.556 --> 00:23:10.432
Just like...

00:23:10.516 --> 00:23:13.602
Just like we are now.

00:23:13.686 --> 00:23:20.526
But maybe I'm the one who's lonely now.

00:23:20.609 --> 00:23:22.903
You won't be lonely.

00:23:22.987 --> 00:23:25.572
You're going to forget everything.

00:23:25.656 --> 00:23:28.909
Junko Ogami will never have existed.

00:23:28.993 --> 00:23:33.038
That's what happens with Torches.

00:23:33.122 --> 00:23:34.999
Here.

00:23:35.082 --> 00:23:36.667
Look inside.

00:23:51.724 --> 00:23:54.727
I couldn't completely fix it.

00:23:54.810 --> 00:23:57.479
There was one that I just couldn't find.

00:23:57.563 --> 00:24:04.153
So I used the ring you gave me as
a present when you were little instead.

00:24:04.236 --> 00:24:07.197
It was a toy, but you called it a gem.

00:24:43.317 --> 00:24:44.777
I'm sorry...

00:24:56.622 --> 00:24:57.998
Mm.

00:25:13.555 --> 00:25:17.226
She wasn't really angry.
She was in a good mood.

00:25:22.439 --> 00:25:24.525
I'm not upset at all.

00:25:26.485 --> 00:25:28.070
I'm so glad...

00:25:30.572 --> 00:25:33.409
Now this is where I smile.

00:25:33.492 --> 00:25:38.747
This is just how it is for Torches...

00:25:40.207 --> 00:25:42.418
...and for Flame Hazes.

00:25:44.878 --> 00:25:51.718
Say, Hamaguchi-kun and
I should come here sometime...

00:26:04.690 --> 00:26:10.696
<i>We held on to feelings
we couldn't give up</i>

00:26:10.779 --> 00:26:16.785
<i>Even so, we've walked this far</i>

00:26:16.869 --> 00:26:24.334
<i>It's like we haven't made any progress,
and have only slightly touched</i>

00:26:24.418 --> 00:26:30.257
a <i>wish carried</i> by <i>the waves of time</i>

00:26:30.340 --> 00:26:36.513
<i>Visiting distant memories</i>

00:26:36.597 --> 00:26:46.899
<i>I feel like things shine with,
"This wasn't how it was"</i>

00:26:46.982 --> 00:26:54.531
<i>After getting through that bright day</i>

00:26:54.615 --> 00:26:56.825
<i>we're here now</i>

00:26:56.909 --> 00:27:06.835
<i>In this place where endings
and beginnings don't exist</i>

00:27:06.919 --> 00:27:09.213
<i>I am sure we will now</i>

00:27:09.296 --> 00:27:21.183
<i>walk again and discover a new dream</i>
